Z||000005||maryjane||10-12-2001||09:27 PM||||Allrighty. I first tried this at a little place in Snook, Tex. A place called Sodalak's Restraunt. Not much there but a convience store, Sodalak's, and lots of oil wells. The Texas legislature gave em some sort of award & it was in the local paper, so I checked it out on my way to East Texas one night. Do a google search on chicken fried bacon. It works best with thick bacon. Mix milk, (I use canned evapoated milk) egg and any seasoning you like. Pour some flour out on a plate or wax paper. dip the bacon in the liquid, then kinda drag in thru the flour. do it twice for good coating. Then, you just deep fry it as you would onion rings or french fries. It will pop like crazy so be carefull Or, you can make up a mixture like you would use for onion rings, where milk, flour,egg, and seasonings are all mixed together, then dip the bacon in it and fry it in oil.  I've tried broiling it, not too good, sticks too much and you pull all the breading off. Last,, make an appointment to have your cholesterol checked.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>1 egg<BR>2 cups milk<BR>1/2 tea sp of chili powder<BR>1/4 tea spoon black pepper <BR>2 cups self-rising flour<BR>Don't add salt- salt ain't good for ya <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||1
